      "title": "CylinderGeometry",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DescriptionSpec": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "How a type becomes geometry.\n\n``xacro_macro`` is how a vendor description is incorporated **without editing\nit** — the open question L1 leaves for the component library. The generator's\nentire knowledge of the vendor package is the argument names below, which are\nmodel data. It never opens a vendor file and never patches one, so a vendor\nupgrade that renames a parameter is a two-line model diff.",
      "properties": {
        "body": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Body"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "bound_args": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "macro parameter -> generator binding name; an unknown binding is an error",
          "title": "Bound Args",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "file": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "File"
        },
        "fixed_args": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "number"
              }
            ]
          },
          "title": "Fixed Args",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "macro": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Macro"
        },
        "package": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Package"
        },
        "provider": {
          "enum": [
            "xacro_macro",
            "body"
          ],
          "title": "Provider",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "provider"
      ],
      "title": "DescriptionSpec",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "GraspSpec": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "How this end effector grasps: the stroke it has, and what a skill commands.\n\nOne audience, on both paths. Every value here is read by the L3 skill server\nin simulation and on hardware alike; none of it is simulation-only. That is a\nchange from what this block used to be. It also carried\n`attach_link_suffix`, `closed_threshold_rad` and `open_threshold_rad`, which\nexisted solely to configure the contact-triggered attachment plugin ADR-0023\nintroduced. That plugin is gone — superseded on the evidence of the 84-trial\nfriction campaign in `docs/measurements/2026-08-25-friction-grasp/`, which\nmeasured it firing at first pad contact and destroying the very stall this\nblock exists to produce — so the fields that fed it are gone with it.\n\nWhat remains is one stroke described once: where the joint travels, how fast,\nhow its angle maps to a pad opening, and how wide to close by default. A\ngrasp is now evidenced the way ADR-0022 always said it was — the pads meet\nthe part, the joint stops short of its command, and the controller reports a\nstall.",
      "properties": {
        "closed_position": {
          "default": 0.85,
          "title": "Closed Position",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "default_grasp_width_m": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "exclusiveMinimum": 0.0,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Default Grasp Width M"
        },
        "drive_joint_suffix": {
          "title": "Drive Joint Suffix",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "follower_max_rate_rad_s": {
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Follower Max Rate Rad S",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "linkage": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/GripperLinkage"
        },
        "max_drive_rate_rad_s": {
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Max Drive Rate Rad S",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "open_position": {
          "default": 0.0,
          "title": "Open Position",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "drive_joint_suffix",
        "max_drive_rate_rad_s",
        "follower_max_rate_rad_s",
        "linkage"
      ],
      "title": "GraspSpec",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "GripperLinkage": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Where a parallel gripper's pads are, as a function of its drive angle.\n\nTwo maps, one crank. Across the tool axis::\n\n    opening(q) = 2 * (drive_pivot_y_m - pad_inset_m\n                      + finger_offset_y_m*cos(q) - finger_offset_z_m*sin(q))\n\nand along it, how far PROXIMAL of the planning tip link the centre of the pad\nface sits::\n\n    pad_plane_offset(q) = tip_link_z_m - drive_pivot_z_m - pad_face_centre_z_m\n                          - (finger_offset_y_m*sin(q)\n                             + finger_offset_z_m*cos(q))\n\nThis is the single home of both relationships (P1). The L3 skill server\nreceives these seven numbers through the generated bring-up plan and\nevaluates the same closed forms, so task-space widths and task-space *poses*\nmean the same thing in the model, in the validator, and on the robot.\n\nThey are closed forms rather than fits or tables because they are derivable:\nthe drive joint and the finger joint rotate about opposite axes by the same\nangle, so their rotations cancel, the pad face stays parallel to the tool\naxis, and only its origin translates. The two maps are that one translation\nresolved on two axes — which is also why they belong in one model rather than\ntwo, since separating them would mean a second copy of the crank.\n\nEvery field is a dimension in the robot's own description, which is what makes\nan audit possible: each can be checked against the vendor URDF or mesh rather\nthan taken on trust.",
      "properties": {
        "drive_pivot_y_m": {
          "title": "Drive Pivot Y M",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "drive_pivot_z_m": {
          "title": "Drive Pivot Z M",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "finger_offset_y_m": {
          "title": "Finger Offset Y M",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "finger_offset_z_m": {
          "title": "Finger Offset Z M",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "pad_face_centre_z_m": {
          "title": "Pad Face Centre Z M",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "pad_inset_m": {
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Pad Inset M",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "tip_link_z_m": {
          "title": "Tip Link Z M",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "drive_pivot_y_m",
        "drive_pivot_z_m",
        "finger_offset_y_m",
        "finger_offset_z_m",
        "pad_inset_m",
        "tip_link_z_m",
        "pad_face_centre_z_m"
      ],
      "title": "GripperLinkage",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "HardwareBackend": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One selectable ``ros2_control`` backend for a type.\n\nThe plugin class string exists exactly once, here. That is what makes\n'the only thing that differs is which plugin is loaded' (ADR-0005) true by\nconstruction rather than by discipline.",
      "properties": {
        "instance_params": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Instance Params",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "ros2_control_plugin": {
          "title": "Ros2 Control Plugin",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "ros2_control_plugin"
      ],
      "title": "HardwareBackend",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Inertial": {
